{{Quote|I didn't know Mandalorians developed a type of lightsaber.''"<br />"''We didn't. This was one of a kind. Legend tells that it was created over a thousand years ago by Tarre Vizsla, the first Mandalorian ever inducted into the Jedi Order. After his passing, the Jedi kept the saber in their temple. That was until members of House Vizsla snuck in and liberated it. They used the saber to unify the people and strike down those who would oppose them. One time, they ruled all of Mandalore wielding this blade.|[[Kanan Jarrus]] and [[Fenn Rau]], on the Darksaber|<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />}}
'''Tarre Vizsla''' {{Pronounced|file=TarreVizsla-ArtHistory.flac|tär 'vɪzlə}}, was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Mandalorian]] who was the first of his people to be inducted into the [[Jedi Order]] as a [[Jedi Initiate|child]] around [[1,050 BBY|1050 BBY]]. Vizsla became a [[Jedi Knight]] and created the [[Darksaber]], a unique [[Color|black]]-bladed [[lightsaber]] which would become the symbol of leadership within [[House Vizsla]] and became the [[Mandalore (title)|ruler]] of [[Mandalore]]. He was also the ancestor of [[Pre Vizsla]], [[Paz Vizsla]], and his son [[Ragnar Vizsla]].

==Biography==
===Jedi and Mand'alor===
{{Quote|It was forged over 1,000 years ago by the Mandalore Tarre Vizsla. He was both Mandalorian and Jedi.|[[The Armorer]] explaining the origin of the Darksaber to [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Chapter 5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>}}
[[File:MandoDarksaber-SWGoH.png|thumb|left|200px|The Darksaber, a unique black-bladed lightsaber.]]
Tarre Vizsla was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who,<ref name="Complete Season Three">[[Star Wars Rebels: Complete Season Three|''Star Wars Rebels'': Complete Season Three]], "Trials of the Darksaber" DVD commentary</ref> was inducted into the [[Jedi Order]] around [[1,050 BBY|1050 BBY]], becoming the first [[Mandalorian]] to do so.<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Tarre eventually became a famous [[Jedi Knight]].<ref name="TOM 104">{{GermanFanCite|104|Database}}</ref> Vizsla created the [[Darksaber]] during his [[time]] as a [[Jedi]]. A unique [[Color|black]]-colored [[lightsaber]]<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> with a hilt forged from high&ndash;quality [[beskar]],<ref name="Chapter 5" /> the Darksaber became the symbol of leadership for [[House Vizsla]],<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> the [[Mandalorian house]] that Tarre founded,<ref name="Chapter 5" /> of the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]]. Tarre Vizsla led his people with the [[Sword|saber]],<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> eventually becoming his planet's [[Mandalore (title)|Mand'alor]].<ref name="Art History">{{FOD|Art History}}</ref> The house he formed eventually also produced a smaller subgroup, [[Clan Vizsla]].<ref name="Chapter 5" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Well, you were just a baby so you couldn't come, but father brought me here to see the statue of Tarre Vizsla, the ancient Mandalorian ruler.|Sabine Wren, to Tristan Wren|<ref name="Art History" />}}
[[File:Tarre_Vizsla.png|thumb|right|250px|Tarre Vizsla wielding the Darksaber]]
After Vizsla's [[Death|passing]], the Darksaber was kept in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] until it was [[Sacking of the Jedi Temple|taken]] by members of [[Mandalorian house|House]] Vizsla<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> during the [[fall of the Old Republic]]<ref name="Mandalore Plot">{{TCW|The Mandalore Plot}}</ref> and was used to unite Mandalore.<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> Sometime after his death, a large [[Statue of Tarre Vizsla|statue]] was erected on Mandalore to remember his legacy. When the Mandalorian [[Sabine Wren]] was young, her [[Parent|father]], [[Alrich Wren]], brought her to the statue to appreciate its history and legacy. During the [[Mandalorian Civil War (Imperial Era)|Mandalorian Civil War]] of the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Galactic Empire]] desecrated the statue and Vizsla's memory by constructing an outpost on it, covering various parts of the statue including its face. Not willing to allow the Empire to disrespect what it stood for, Sabine and her younger brother, [[Tristan Wren]] destroyed the outpost, bringing the statue back to its former appearance.<ref name="Art History" /> Tarre Vizsla's descendant, [[Paz Vizsla]], [[Fight for the Darksaber|fought]] fellow Mandalorian [[Din Djarin]] for the Darksaber, but failed.<ref name="Chapter 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
Tarre Vizsla first appeared in a flashback in the episode "[[Trials of the Darksaber]]," the fifteenth episode of the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|third season]] of ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' which aired in [[2017]].<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />

